From 7917d46a2af38b53e5d2f0088449cc7920744879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:41:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sync): exclude macOS DarkWake from replica stale budget
 [daveey]

Problem: MacBook filed t_a665a3d62ef843cc at 17:43:23 PST during
lid-closed sleep; full Wake was 17:50:17, recovery within 141s.
Why 1: replica remained behind during short maintenance rounds.
Why 2: monotonic advances in DarkWake, unlike full sleep.
Root (happened): detector equated monotonic uptime with sync opportunity.
Root (not caught): sleep tests froze monotonic and never modeled DarkWake;
previous live verification called a stale replica a true positive without
checking full-wake evidence. Recurrence: cron reruns already use the shared
host_fully_awake probe; outbox gate PR3255 has the same known limitation.

Reuse cron probe lazily once per check; injectable awake_fn. Persist last
observation and excluded seconds, migrating old memo records, and report
excluded seconds in telemetry and card diagnostics. Both accepted limits:
idle lid-closed AC/external-display Macs and idle lid-open battery Macs
read not fully awake until user activity. Probe failure reads awake;
non-Mac probe does not spawn. No wake_clock or cron implementation change.

Proof: inline pmset timeline from verified source SHA
2d04d37ae866af23199cb17a4c0f5e9ec1d74aa4e310ff4e0d9c72cad7d7258a
first failed unchanged production code with one card at 17:43 PT, then
passed with zero. Persistence test first failed missing last, then passed.
39 replica tests plus 61 unchanged cron tests pass; scripts/check 20 OK.
The 33 full DarkWakes total 1299s; alarm occurs 7s into final 45s wake,
so fixture counts only elapsed prefix then remaining time after alarm.
Sampling schedule is modeled explicitly; pmset does not contain ticks.

Task t_823c0a5431d5993d retains outbox exclusion and installed hub/Mac proof.
Prevention not yet observed live. No soak or forced wake.
